meia_data:tech_tactical_microgrid a bfo:MaterialEntity ;
    rdfs:label "Tactical Micro-Grid Hybrid Energy & Storage System" ;
    skos:related meia_data:meia_ExpeditionaryEnergy,
        meia_data:osra_PowerAndEnergyStorage ;
    meia:ADDRESSES_JOP meia_data:tech_jop_tactical_microgrid ;
    meia:DEVELOPED_BY meia_data:org_t2s_solutions ;
    meia:EVALUATED_BY meia_data:crm_submission_27268 ;
    meia:HAS_READINESS_ASSESSMENT meia_data:eval_tactical_microgrid_readiness ;
    meia:description "T2S Solutions has been developing a Counter Surveillance Reconnaissance (CSR) Increment 1 prototype since October 2024. This effort was funded by the competitively awarded Multi-Domain Multi-Tier System of Systems Prototyping OTA contract aligned to the former All Domain Sensing Cross Functional Team. Intent for Increment 1 is to deliver the prototype to the PdM TSS in 4QFY26 for follow-on use by Army space formations to assist with incremental development and accelerate POR fielding schedule outlined in the CSR ACDD development timelines. T2S conducted system component research and assessment and gained ADS CFT approval for baseline component configuration. Both PdL TSS and TID-SS (formerly ACM SHA) concurred with the recommended system configuration. The prototype consists of a C2 orchestrator that integrates a Mission Planning Tool (MPT) and various effectors. Activities to date have validated message traffic routing from the MPT at JWICS, through a guard to the Orchestrator at both SIPR and SBU and to an effector controller. This architecture validates cross domain connectivity at both classified and unclassified levels. T2S is developing Inc. 1 with warfighter input. T2S is integrated with 1MDTF’s Innovation Working Group and incorporating their feedback in the development. T2S has had multiple engagements with 1MDTF and USARPAC and was onboarded to the MDO Live IATT in March 2026. The Inc 1 was also onboarded to the JMC IATT in April 2026 to support demonstration at PCC6 in July 2026. The MDO Live IATT is valid until January 2027 which will support follow-on experimentation and incremental development with the 1MDTF." ;
    meia:differentiator "Government owned solution that can integrate effectors from multiple vendors. As new counter sensing effectors come online, only a low level of effort will be required to integrate the new capabilities. Providing only the coordination and orchestration allows T2S to work with the government to select best of breed effectors. The solution provided does not lock the government into a specific vendor and" ;
    meia:graphDomain "TECH" ;
    meia:hasEpistemicClaim meia_data:claim_eval_tactical_microgrid_readiness_trl,
        meia_data:claim_tech_jop_tactical_microgrid ;
    meia:irl "7" ;
    meia:mrl "3" ;
    meia:offering_name "Tactical Micro-Grid Hybrid Energy & Storage System" ;
    meia:raw_offering_name "Counter Sensing" ;
    meia:trl "5" ;
    meia:type "Prototype" .

meia_data:tech_voltvessel_energy a bfo:MaterialEntity ;
    rdfs:label "VoltVessel Maritime High-Density Energy Module" ;
    skos:related meia_data:meia_ContestedLogistics,
        meia_data:osra_PowerAndEnergyStorage ;
    meia:ADDRESSES_JOP meia_data:tech_jop_voltvessel_energy ;
    meia:DEVELOPED_BY meia_data:org_voltage_vessels ;
    meia:EVALUATED_BY meia_data:crm_submission_25615 ;
    meia:HAS_READINESS_ASSESSMENT meia_data:eval_voltvessel_energy_readiness ;
    meia:description "Voltage Vessels delivers the Eclipse X9 Expeditionary Manufacturing Cell, a forward additive manufacturing capability for rapid production and repair of rugged composite mission hardware in contested and distributed environments. The system is built around Eclipse X9, a reinforced thermoplastic composite feedstock engineered for harsh-environment performance, structural stability, and repairability. It is intended to produce mission-relevant parts such as payload housings, battery compartments, sensor mounts, electronics enclosures, protective shrouds, brackets, covers, and other field-replaceable components for unmanned and expeditionary systems. The capability combines feedstock readiness, additive manufacturing, post-processing and inspection, and digital thread / configuration control into a repeatable workflow that can be deployed closer to the point of need. This reduces dependence on long supply chains, lowers sustainment burden, and enables rapid iteration and localized replacement of critical hardware." ;
    meia:differentiator "Voltage’s differentiator is that it is not just a printer or just a material. It is a mission-focused hardware production capability built around a rugged composite platform, controlled manufacturing workflow, and field repair logic. Eclipse X9 is designed for harsh operational environments and offers a combination of structural performance, low water absorption, corrosion resistance, non-conductive behavior, and repairability that is well suited to distributed sustainment and unmanned system hardware. The capability is designed to scale through standardized feedstock, repeatable process parameters, and part-library driven production rather than one-off prototyping. Unlike traditional supply models that rely on long lead times and brittle replacement chains, Voltage enables localized manufacture and rapid regeneration of small but mission-critical parts at the point of need. That makes it directly relevant to contested logistics, where tempo is often lost not because entire platforms fail, but because simple structural and packaging components are unavailable or slow to replace." ;
    meia:graphDomain "TECH" ;
    meia:hasEpistemicClaim meia_data:claim_eval_voltvessel_energy_readiness_trl,
        meia_data:claim_tech_jop_voltvessel_energy ;
    meia:irl "7" ;
    meia:mrl "9" ;
    meia:offering_name "VoltVessel Maritime High-Density Energy Module" ;
    meia:raw_offering_name "Eclipse X9 Distributed Composite Manufacturing for Austere Logistics" ;
    meia:trl "8" ;
    meia:type "Product" .

