meia_data:tech_ghostfin_uuv a bfo:MaterialEntity ;
    rdfs:label "Ghostfin: Long-Range, Hybrid Electric Medium UUV" ;
    skos:related meia_data:meia_CollaborativeAutonomy,
        meia_data:meia_CounterC5ISRT,
        meia_data:osra_UnmannedUnderwaterVehicles ;
    meia:ADDRESSES_JOP meia_data:tech_jop_ghostfin_uuv ;
    meia:CLAIMS_CAPABILITY meia_data:tech_ghostfin_endurance,
        meia_data:tech_ghostfin_payload,
        meia_data:tech_ghostfin_portability,
        meia_data:tech_ghostfin_propulsion,
        meia_data:tech_ghostfin_range ;
    meia:DEVELOPED_BY meia_data:org_albacore ;
    meia:EVALUATED_BY meia_data:crm_submission_26705 ;
    meia:HAS_READINESS_ASSESSMENT meia_data:eval_ghostfin_uuv_readiness ;
    meia:PARTICIPATED_IN_DEMO meia_data:demo_afsim_ghostfin,
        meia_data:demo_nswc_pc_purchase,
        meia_data:demo_repmus_26,
        meia_data:demo_silent_swarm_26,
        meia_data:demo_sonic_spear_26 ;
    meia:description "Ghostfin is a long-range, hybrid-electric unmanned undersea vehicle (UUV) designed and built in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania. The vehicle is capable of transiting more than 1,000 nautical miles, remaining at sea for up to 30 days, and carrying up to 250 pounds of configurable mission payload. Ghostfin is capable of four-person launch and recovery, shipboard launch, underwater launch from a dry-deck shelter, and air delivery, enabling flexible employment across a range of operational environments. Ghostfin extends UUV reach beyond traditional operating envelopes and enables distributed effects at operationally significant ranges. Its modular payload bay can accommodate Albacore-provided, vendor-provided, and Government-provided payloads, supporting mission sets including ISR, kinetic one-way attack, mine countermeasures, anti-submarine warfare, counter-UUV operations, and electronic and non-kinetic attack. This flexibility allows operators to hold adversary forces and maritime infrastructure at risk while reducing exposure to high-value manned platforms, providing a high-performance, scalable capability for maritime operations." ;
    meia:differentiator "Ghostfin’s technology centers on a compact hybrid-electric power system, comprised of a JP-8 combustion engine and batteries, specifically designed for small and medium UUVs, overcoming the fundamental limitations that have historically constrained battery-only UUV platforms. This represents a significant engineering advancement, as hybrid-electric systems have previously been limited to much larger UUV platforms due to size and complexity constraints. This capability enables a 10-20x improvement in range compared with battery-powered sUUV platforms and a 5-10x range improvement compared with battery-powered mUUVs, despite a significantly reduced size. Ghostfin also features a modular payload bay capable of carrying up to 250 pounds, allowing rapid reconfiguration across mission sets. Albacore has currently developed its own ISR, kinetic defeat, and minesweeping payloads for Ghostfin. Government-provided and other vendor-provided payloads can also easily be integrated into Ghostfin. This payload flexibility enables a single platform to support evolving operational needs without redesigning the vehicle." ;
    meia:graphDomain "TECH" ;
    meia:hasEpistemicClaim meia_data:claim_demo_afsim_ghostfin,
        meia_data:claim_demo_nswc_pc_purchase,
        meia_data:claim_demo_repmus_26,
        meia_data:claim_demo_silent_swarm_26,
        meia_data:claim_demo_sonic_spear_26,
        meia_data:claim_eval_ghostfin_uuv_readiness_trl,
